-- SessionRuntimeEvent(type='text_delta', data={'content': 'Verification 
passed.\n\n## Change\n\n`src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx`\n- Replaced the one-shot
`setTimeout` in the mount effect with a `schedule(onDone)` helper that clears 
any pending timer before arming a new 120 ms timer, plus `clearScheduled()` for 
unmount cleanup (single `timerRef`, so no overlapping timers are possible).\n- 
Added `retry()`: sets state to `loading` synchronously (panel immediately shows 
`Checking service…`), then schedules the same 120 ms delay resolving to 
`success` (`All changes are synced.`), regardless of `?sync=error` still being 
in the URL. It\'s a `type="button"` with local state only — no 
navigation/reload, and no parent/task-selection state is touched.\n- Added the 
`Retry sync` button inside the existing `role="alert"` error block; it only 
exists in the error branch, so the success path at `/` never renders it and it 
disappears after success.\n\n`src/styles.css`\n- Added `.sync-retry { 
justify-self: start; margin-top: 6px; }` so the button aligns within the 
existing error grid; existing global button styling, focus-visible outline, and 
error/success colors are untouched.\n\n## Commands actually 
run\n\n`verify_frontend` → `npm run verify:agent` (`npm run build && npm run 
test:public`): exit 0 — tsc + vite build succeeded, 6/6 public Playwright tests 
passed.\n\n## Remaining risks\n\n- The retry result is hard-coded to success 
(per the acceptance criteria), so retrying while `/` is actually served 
`?sync=error` will report success; if the intent is to re-probe the URL, that\'s
a follow-up.\n- No new automated test covers the retry flow (existing public 
tests were left untouched by design); it was verified only via build + existing 
suite, not by a dedicated browser assertion.', 'aid': 0})
